      "summary": "H3 is a minimal H(TTP) framework built for high performance and portability.",
      "details": "H3 is a minimal H(TTP) framework built for high performance and portability. Prior to 1.15.5, there is a critical HTTP Request Smuggling vulnerability. readRawBody is doing a strict case-sensitive check for the Transfer-Encoding header. It explicitly looks for \"chunked\", but per the RFC, this header should be case-insensitive. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.5.",
